# Force LF for shell/SQL scripts regardless of any individual clone's own
# core.autocrlf setting. Found live, 2026-09-09 (DUTD2 Gate 2, first-ever
# real UI-driven update test for HCopilot): release-src/scripts/update_offline.sh
# had CRLF line endings even though the actual committed blob is clean LF --
# this Windows checkout's own core.autocrlf=true silently re-introduces
# CRLF into the working tree on checkout, without a .gitattributes forcing
# the real, stored line ending, while `git status` reports clean (autocrlf
# normalizes the comparison, not the on-disk bytes) -- invisible until the
# Platform first actually executed the file directly via its own shebang
# line, which the Linux kernel parses literally including the trailing \r
# ("env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory"). Same real bug class already
# hit and fixed this way for Voice Project (Bug 24) -- mirrored exactly
# rather than re-derived.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
